    "level": 1,
    "paras": [
     "Anolis charlesmyersi is a species of lizard in the family Dactyloidae. The species is native to Central America."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Etymology",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The specific name, charlesmyersi, is in honor of American herpetologist Charles William Myers."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Geographic range",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "A. charlesmyersi is found in Costa Rica and Panama."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Habitat",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The preferred natural habitat of A. charlesmyersi is forest."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Description",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "A. charlesmyersi is medium-sized for its genus. Adults may attain a snout-to-vent length (SVL) of about 7.5 cm (3.0 in). The tail is relatively short, 1 – 1.5 times SVL. The hind legs are very short for the genus. The dewlap is brick red, with rows of white spots."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Reproduction",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "A. charlesmyersi is oviparous."
    ]
   }
